Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?PUBLISH-FIX-93:=20the=20gate=20learner's=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?evidence=20rule=20=E2=80=94=20review=20finding=20F1,=20and=20it?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20reverses=20FIX-91?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Blind application review, revision 34a25ad2, learning reliability 4.5/10. F1: the training filter
accepted a look as evidence for one flow gate when every NON-flow gate passed, even if sibling flow
gates refused it; evaluateUnit then called those looks 'newly admitted' after moving one line. A
promotion moves ONE line, so those looks would still not trade. Reviewer's reproduction: 1,100 looks
at FI15 0.15 with RV60 failing published FI15=0.15 and admitted none of them. That filter was
PUBLISH-FIX-91, added the same afternoon to stop the learner starving.

Corroborated by our own 48-hour gate study (3,174 scored looks): FI15 was never the only refusal on
any look, so the entire cohort FIX-91 added for FI15 was looks the complete policy still refuses.

- othersOk is strict again (every other required gate actually passed; ok !== true is never
  counterfactually passable) and is the ONLY thing promotion counts. FIX-91's wider set survives as
  familyOk, reported in evidence and in the log line, never counted.
- costHurdlePct fallback 1.0 -> 1.8: it still carried the superseded 0.4%/side schedule after FIX-84
  moved the paper account to the real Kraken Tier-1 taker of 0.80%. fly.js derives 1.8 from the
  running policy, so the live learner was correct; any caller that could not read the policy was
  certifying moves against half the real cost.
- minClusters 12 -> 30 (review: 'it can certify a lesson using much less effective evidence than the
  label implies'). A bootstrap over twelve coin-hours reads confident on noise. Can only prevent a
  move, never cause one.
- the GATE LEARNING log line now prints scored, usable and the family count it does not count.

Follow-up ticket: gates that fail together need a JOINT family policy proposed and forward-tested
against the complete rule set. A single-gate threshold change cannot honestly move them.

Tests: publish-fix-93-joint-policy-evidence 5/5 (FIX93-2 is the reviewer's reproduction; FIX93-5
guards the shipped bars). learning-gate-lesson 10/10 and publish-fix-84 4/4 updated to the corrected
law. No line can move in production meanwhile: the live learner reads USABLE_57_OF_1000.

